    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0118" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg58"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Bancroft.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 105.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 7, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your dispatch of the 20th November, No. 85,
                    has been received. I am greatly obliged to you for having placed before me in so
                    clear a light the tendencies of existing European interests in favor of the
                    continuance of peace between North Germany and France. Certainly all friends of
                    progress and civilization must share with you in deprecating a conflict the mere
                    apprehension of which has produced universal anxiety in Europe.</p>
                <pb facs="0119" n="59" xml:id="pg59"/>
                <p>The procrastination of reconstruction in Spain seems now to forbode a civil war
                    in the peninsula. It is not believed that other nations of western Europe can
                    feel sufficiently at their ease, in view of such a conflict upon ideas, to
                    engage in contests for mere political advantage or supremacy.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">George Bancroft,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
